      <div type="clause" n="53.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 53.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hit tihtle sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/>, ⁊ lad forberste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.10"/>, bisceop þonne wealde ⁊ stiðlice deme.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf hit tihtla beo, ⁊ lad forbersta, ðonne wealde se bisceop ⁊ stiðlice deme.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hit tihtle sy, ⁊ lad forberste, biscop þonne wealde ⁊ stiðlice deme.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si compellatio sit, et in emundando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.6"/> miseueniat (<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.7"/>probata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.8"/> fuerit), sit in episcopi potestate, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.9"/> ipse grauiter iudicet.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Si autem negauerit et purgare se uoluerit, et in iudicio ceciderit, episcopus uideat et districte iudicet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.3"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>[53, 1] Quodsi inficiata fuerit et purgamine defecerit, cadat in manus episcopi, qui inde acriter iudicet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="53.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="202" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf hit tihtla beo ⁊ lad forbersta, ðonne wealde se<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_53-1.robnote.fn.3"/> bisceop ⁊ stiðlice deme.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif hit tihtle sig and lad forberste, bisceop þonne wealde and stiðlice deme.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn es jedoch [nur] eine [leugbare] Anklage ist, und die Reinigung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.de.1"/> misslingt, dann verfüge der Bischof<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.de.2"/> und richte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_53-1.lnote.de.3"/> streng.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If, however, it is [only] a [deniable] accusation, and the clearing [oath] fails, then let the bishop dispose and judge strictly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="203" ed="#robertson"/>And if a charge is brought and the attempt to refute it fails, the decision shall then rest with the bishop<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_53-1.robnote.n.1"/>, and his judgment shall be strict.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>And if an accusation is brought, and the exculpation fails, the bishop is then to take control and to judge sternly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="283" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if there is an accusation and the oath of exculpation fails, the bishop shall judge and he is to judge harshly.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 349, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">bisceop: se bisceop B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">emendatione</hi> <hi rend="italic">K</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vgl. unten</hi> 56, 1]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">emendatione</hi> K [cf. below 56, 1]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">id est <hi rend="italic">fügt zu T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">id est added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. f. <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Dm T; fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. f. written above Dm T; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et i. g. i. <hi rend="italic">aus THkBr; fehlt KDmR</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et i. g. i. from THkBr; lacking in KDmR</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rst, biscop <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rst, biscop Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so S;</hi> uindicet <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus S; uindicet the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ordal zur Probe ehelicher Treue kommt in Geschichte und Volkskunde zwar oft vor. Doch ist die Übs. von <hi rend="italic">lad</hi> durch <hi rend="italic">iudicium</hi> in Inst zu eng; jenes umfasst auch Reinigungseid</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The ordeal as a test of marital fidelity does indeed occur often in history and folklore. Nevertheless the translation of <hi rend="italic">lad</hi> by <hi rend="italic">iudicium</hi> in Inst is too narrow; the former also includes the oath of exculpation</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Ehegericht 3, also ohne Leibesstrafe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Ehegericht 3, thus without corporal punishment</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_53-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Geistliches Gericht 14a. Das ‘Richten’ bed. nur ‘Bestimmen der Strafe’, nachdem weltlicher Prozess samt landrechtlichem Beweise und Schuldspruch durch bürgerliches Gericht veranging; ebenso <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 56, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Geistliches Gericht 14a. ‘Judging’ means only ‘determining the punishment’, after a secular trial, together with proof according to the law of the land and verdict, had taken place before the civil court; likewise <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 56, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_53-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See P. and M. <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. p. 367.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_53-1.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><label>his</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
